                <pb facs="0476" n="391" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg391"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.1511/108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Charge of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-24T10:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1919, 10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            October 25, 11.50 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>… The President also asked me if possible to secure from the Department an
                    expression of the attitude of the Department towards his administration and
                    approval of official acts to date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
